# AFW value memory

Use when changing value lifetime, reference count, create/allocate APIs, data type bindings, const objects/strings, pools/scopes, or debugging leaks for **long-running scripts**.

**Live maps:** rails [`designs/issue-2-hold-in-inf.md`](../../designs/issue-2-hold-in-inf.md); two worlds [`designs/experiment-brainstorm.md`](../../designs/experiment-brainstorm.md) ([#277](https://github.com/afw-org/afw/issues/277) closed); eval `p` [`designs/experiment-eval-p.md`](../../designs/experiment-eval-p.md) (PR **#287**). 08-21 story [`designs/issue-2-lifetime.md`](../../designs/issue-2-lifetime.md) is history. When they disagree, those live pads win over this rule.

## Pool and scope model

- **Two impls:** heap and tracker (mt = lock wrappers on heap). APR is the reservoir. `create()` of a heap parent is a heap; of a tracker parent is a tracker (extra rule). Base/`env->p` is mt heap. `xctx->p` is ST heap (`create_xctx_p`).
- **Heap / tracker:** single-thread heap for evaluation. One compiled_value evaluate creates a heap, scopes use trackers, wrap **releases** the heap (a closure's reference may keep it). **No reparent** on destroy; parent cascade destroys children. Statement eval `p` is `scope->p` when `{ }` has a frame (PR **#287**). Nested empty `{ }` is not a frame.
- `managed_p`: job pools and heap set self; others inherit. Pool-world object/array: `create_unmanaged` / `_new_p` / `_cede_p`. **`create_managed` is a frame** (no pool).
- `compiled_value` owns a dedicated compile pool; evaluation scratch is the heap.
- Scope create/clone start at RC 1 (creator `release`s). `activate` / `deactivate` are stack push/pop. `closure_binding` `get_reference` / `release`. Last `release` at 0 walks `frame_slots[]`. Store-time bind for literals and nested assign is **#35**. Closure create-at-0; face overlay `set` takes the reference for `o.fn = function…`.
- Short scripts: pool + scope bulk free is enough. **Long-running** needs correct managed escape paths (below).

## Lifetimes (inf chooses policy)

- **permanent** — built-in, or lasts for the life of an AFW environment. Usually `static const` with `afw_value_permanent_<dt>_inf`; env-lifetime values may use the same inf. No refcount; `get_reference` returns as-is. Scalar `get_assignable_value` is as-is; object/array `get_assignable_value` is a managed wrapper/clone. No `create_permanent_*` API.
- **managed** — start-at-1 in `xctx->p`. Caller must release. Extra `get_reference` / `get_assignable_value` bump self. Last release `free_memory`s via `xctx->p`. `afw_value_create_managed_<dt>()`.
- **managed_slice** — for `cType` `afw_utf8_t` / `afw_memory_t` only: a view (pointer + length/size) into a **containing managed** value. Header in `xctx->p` (no stored `p`). Create `get_reference`s containing; slice starts at 1; `get_reference` bumps the slice; last release releases containing and `free_memory`s the slice header via `xctx->p`. `afw_value_create_managed_<dt>_slice()`.
- **unmanaged** — programmer-owned; usually created in a pool and lasting for that pool. Scalar and object/array **value** `get_reference` / `release` throw. `get_assignable_value` promotes or clones to managed in `xctx->p` (script `{}` / `[]` clone; runtime/adapter object is a managed look-through wrapper). `afw_value_create_unmanaged_<dt>()` / `allocate_unmanaged_*`.

**Slot fill:** `slot_store` / `as_assignable` / `add_reference` take `xctx` only (no dest `p`). `get_reference` is a bump. `afw_value_clone_or_reference` is a compatibility name for `get_reference`. Clone into a pool is `clone_unmanaged` / `clone_managed`.

Do not invent new lifetime paths; match existing create_* patterns.

**Untrusted external bytes** (process env, FCGI params): never wrap as string without validation. Use **`afw_value_create_from_external_octets` / `_z`** (string if valid UTF-8 else hexBinary). See **`afw-environment-variables`**.

## Active long-running focus

- Implement/complete **optional_release** / **get_reference** on escaping values: objects, arrays, closures, `compiled_value`, and other managed kinds that outlive a scope.
- Evaluation temporaries use **`scope->p`** when `{ }` has a frame (PR **#287**). Heap free-list mixed sizes is **withdrawn** as the remaining eval win (re-measured after #287). Remaining long-running soaks: `function_return` (FRV wrapper left in caller `p`) and `array_push_pop` (managed ring entry in `xctx->p`) — live table [`src/afw/tests-extra/issue-2/01-rss-hard-loops/README.md`](../../src/afw/tests-extra/issue-2/01-rss-hard-loops/README.md).
- Heap tracker + last-release walk handle bulk release. **No reparent** on destroy. Polish value-inf hooks; do not replace the pool kinds.
- **Qualifier snapshots** (`qualifier()` / `qualifiers()`, issue **#9**) allocate **fresh, possibly large** memory objects (`environment::`, `request::`, nested `qualifiers()`). Prefer `qualifier::name` for normal work; treat repeated/retained snapshots as long-running stress — see **`afw-qualified-variables`**, `beta-backlog.md`.

## Shared mutables and defaults (issue #110 class)

- **Permanent** values and some **compiled literals** (`{}`, `[]`, const objects) may be **shared** across evaluations or requests. Script may still mutate object/array contents via property assignment.
- Built-ins that **return a default** for a missing property/variable/key must not hand back a shared mutable without **`afw_value_clone` into the call/result pool** (`afw-function`). Residual properties or use-after-free show up on the **second** request in long-running hosts.
- Prefer unit tests that mutate one returned default and assert a later call gets a clean default (`afw-adaptive-script`, `afw-tests`). Multi-request free paths: `afwdev test --env-mode valgrind` and/or `afwfcgi`.

## Source of truth and producers

- Metadata: `generate/objects/_AdaptiveDataTypeGenerate_/*.json` (`cType`, `special`, `scalar`, `directReturn`, …).
- Generator of infs + create APIs: `_afwdev/generate/data_type_bindings.py`.
- **Type × lifetime matrix (phase 0a):** living table and generator decision tree in [`designs/memory-management.md`](../../designs/memory-management.md) under **Phase 0 — 0a** (35 types; families special / utf8 / memory / struct / small-direct / pointer-direct). Use that before changing create/release behavior. Live maps: rails [`designs/issue-2-hold-in-inf.md`](../../designs/issue-2-hold-in-inf.md). 08-21 story is history: [`designs/issue-2-lifetime.md`](../../designs/issue-2-lifetime.md).
- Const permanent instances: `strings.py` (scalar `self_v_*` for supported types), `const_objects.py` (objects + scalar/array props), bindings (ids/empty arrays), `function_bindings.py` (function object wrappers).
- Runtime: core `.so` and extensions call generated `create_managed_*` / `create_unmanaged_*` and reuse permanent pointers (`afw_v_*`, null, empty arrays).
- **Prefer static const Adaptive values over re-create:** use existing `afw_v_*` / `afw_boolean_v_*` / `afw_integer_v_zero|one` / `afw_value_null|undefined` (from `afw_strings.h`, `afw_value.h`, etc.) when the constant already exists. Do not `create_unmanaged_string(afw_s_foo)` or `set_property_as_string(..., afw_s_foo)` only to wrap one — use `afw_object_set_property(..., afw_v_foo, ...)`. `dataType::` lines in `strings.txt` produce typed static const values (`integer::zero` → `afw_integer_v_zero`), distinct from string `"zero"`.
- **Wording in source:** do **not** call these a “catalog” in comments, docs, or generated text. Prefer **static const** / **permanent** values (or point at `afw_strings.h` / `afw_value.h`). Fine in chat; avoid in the tree.

Never hand-edit `generated/` — change generator or JSON, then `./afwdev build --cdev -j`.

## Exploration order

1. `_AdaptiveDataTypeGenerate_` JSON, `data_type_bindings.py` `@details`, and **Phase 0a matrix** in `designs/memory-management.md`
2. `strings.py` / `const_objects.py` permanent emission
3. Hand `src/afw/value/` (e.g. closure_binding) for non-dataType kinds
4. Sample `create_unmanaged_*` call sites in `function/`

